  "id": "social-interest",
  "term": "social interest",
  "definition": "Social interest is a person’s tendency to cooperate with others and feel that they belong in the wider community. In Adlerian psychology, it is viewed as a marker of mental health and is linked with empathy, cooperation, optimism, and better interpersonal relationships, whereas low social interest is associated with self-centeredness, loneliness, and seeking attention.",
